vulnerabilities.suggested_fix:
Add authorization to finalizeUpgrade_v4, e.g.:
- `_auth(MANAGE_NODE_OPERATOR_ROLE)` or an Aragon upgrade/admin role, before executing.

Additionally, consider making the cutoff governance-correctable:
- Remove or relax the monotonicity constraint in _setExitDeadlineThreshold (or gate it to only apply when called through normal updates, not initial initialization), so a mistaken/attacker-set cutoff can be lowered by governance.

Example:
```solidity
function finalizeUpgrade_v4(uint256 _exitDeadlineThresholdInSeconds) external {
    _auth(MANAGE_NODE_OPERATOR_ROLE);
    require(hasInitialized(), "CONTRACT_NOT_INITIALIZED");
    _checkContractVersion(3);
    ...
}
```
